 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Each log is \"<timestamp>,<merchantId>,<statusCode>,<count>\" (logs may be unordered; records with the same key add up). Status 200 is success; every 4xx/5xx code is a distinct error. For each merchant, evaluation happens at each distinct timestamp t where it has records, over its records with t-windowSize+1 <= timestamp <= t. Alerts are strings \"<t>,<merchantId>,<statusCode>\" ordered by t, then merchant (code point), then code. Level 3: same condition as level 2, but alerts can repeat: an alert fires when the condition becomes true for an inactive (merchant, code); the pair becomes inactive again at an evaluation of that merchant where the condition is false.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk04-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
